.TH GITCRAWL 1 gitcrawl-1.0.0
.SH NAME
gitcrawl \- Git-native content-addressable web archival engine and crawler
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B gitcrawl
.I command
[\fIoptions\fR]
[\fIarguments\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B gitcrawl
is a fast, zero-dependency C99 CLI tool that crawls web pages and commits their history
straight into Git repositories as a content-addressable object store.
.PP
It sanitizes dynamic web noise (CSRF tokens, dynamic banners, ads), generates clean,
diff-friendly Markdown for rapid terminal inspection via \fBgit diff\fR, and bypasses
the working tree by writing blobs, trees, and atomic commits directly to \fB.git/objects\fR.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B archive \fIurl\fR
Fetches and archives a single URL into the target Git repository branch.
If \fIurl\fR is omitted and stdin is a pipe, archives stream input.
.TP
.B crawl \fIurl\fR
Recursively crawls a website up to a specified depth and page limit, archiving all pages directly into Git.
.TP
.B diff \fIurl\fR [\fIcommit1\fR] [\fIcommit2\fR]
Shows the clean markdown diff of a URL between two revisions or against the previous commit.
.TP
.B search \fIquery\fR
Searches archived URLs, paths, and historical snapshots with fuzzy score ranking.
.TP
.B log \fIurl\fR
Displays the Git commit history and changelog for a specific URL.
.TP
.B show \fIurl\fR
Prints the archived Markdown, original compressed HTML, or metadata JSON for a URL.
.TP
.B list
Lists all archived endpoints in the repository branch.
.TP
.B gc
Optimizes Git packfiles with delta compression and prunes loose objects.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-b " branch"
Target branch name (default: \fIarchive\fR).
.TP
.BI \-d " directory"
Target Git repository directory (default: \fI.\fR).
.TP
.BI \-m " message"
Custom commit message.
.TP
.BI \-l " depth"
Maximum crawl recursion depth (default: \fI1\fR).
.TP
.BI \-p " max_pages"
Maximum number of pages to crawl (default: \fI50\fR).
.TP
.B \-s
Restrict crawler to the same domain.
.TP
.BI \-f " format"
Output format for \fBshow\fR (\fImd\fR, \fIhtml\fR, or \fIjson\fR).
.TP
.B \-i
Read content from stdin for the specified URL.
.TP
.B \-z
Enable fuzzy search matching.
.TP
.B \-v
Display version information.
.TP
.B \-h
Display help message.
